From: Canonical endpoint audit <audit@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:58:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! net: batch-validate solicited/high-bandwidth SHORTTX
 and coalesce incoming TX bursts

Admit untrusted P2P bursts once under a coalesced publication scope instead of atomic batch then whole-burst retry. Preserve decoded good prefix on later malformed message. Add actual queued-wire prefix and 256-member bad-last work-bound regressions, using per-ATMP PreChecks debug trace. This intentionally trades cross-transaction P2P MSM for bounded adversarial work; RPC atomic batching remains unchanged.
---
